    <main class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-16">
      <header class="mb-12 border-b border-slate-800 pb-8">
        <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-extrabold text-white mb-4">Terms of Service</h1>
        <p class="text-slate-400 text-sm">Last Updated: November 3, 2026</p>
        <p class="text-slate-400 text-sm mt-3">
          These Terms govern your access to and use of the TradeGuard Windows desktop software,
          browser extension, website, and related services.
        </p>
      </header>

      <div class="space-y-12 text-slate-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed">
        <section class="space-y-4">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white"><span class="text-sky-400">1.</span> Acceptance of Terms</h2>
          <p>
            These Terms of Service (the “Terms”) form an agreement between you and the provider identified
            in Section 17 (the “Provider,” “we,” “us,” or “our”). They apply to your access to and use of
            TradeGuard, including the Windows desktop application, browser extension, website, license
            activation system, updates, and related support services (collectively, the “Software”).
          </p>
          <p>
            By purchasing, downloading, installing, activating, or using the Software, you agree to these
            Terms. If you do not agree, do not purchase, install, activate, or use the Software. Before
            completing a purchase, you should have a reasonable opportunity to review and save these Terms.
            Where applicable law requires a separate consent or acknowledgement, including for immediate
            supply of digital content, that consent will be requested separately during checkout.
          </p>
          <p>
            These Terms do not limit any mandatory consumer rights that apply to you under the laws of the
            country or region where you habitually reside.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-4">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white"><span class="text-sky-400">2.</span> Software Description and Risk-Enforcement Notice</h2>
          <p>
            TradeGuard is a self-imposed discipline and risk-management utility. Depending on the version,
            license plan, supported platform, and settings you select, the Software may monitor configured
            risk conditions and restrict local access to supported trading websites or applications when
            those conditions are met.
          </p>
          <div class="bg-slate-800/80 border-l-4 border-amber-500 p-4 rounded-r-lg space-y-2 text-xs md:text-sm">
            <strong class="text-amber-400 font-bold block">Important: Acknowledgement of Lockout Mechanisms</strong>
            <p>
              You understand that restricting access to selected trading platforms is an intentional core
              feature of TradeGuard. When a configured lockout is activated, the Software is designed to
              maintain the restriction for the applicable lockout period. Normal in-app controls may not
              allow you to cancel, bypass, or shorten an active lockout countdown.
            </p>
            <p>
              TradeGuard does not promise an immediate emergency override. If you believe a lockout was
              triggered incorrectly, the Software is malfunctioning, or an exceptional technical issue
              prevents normal use of your computer, you may contact support. We may verify your identity,
              license, device, and the reported circumstances before providing troubleshooting, recovery
              instructions, or other appropriate assistance. Support intervention is assessed case by case
              and is not guaranteed to be immediate or to result in an unlock.
            </p>
            <p>
              Nothing in this section waives a mandatory legal right or prevents you from reporting a
              suspected defect or safety issue.
            </p>
          </div>
          <p>
            TradeGuard operates through supported local software integrations and device-level controls.
            It does not place, execute, cancel, or modify trading orders on your behalf, and it does not
            impose a server-side restriction on your broker or trading platform account. A lockout on one
            device does not necessarily prevent access through another device, browser profile, network,
            application, or account. You remain responsible for understanding these technical limitations.
          </p>
          <p>
            Available risk-management features may vary by Software version, supported platform, operating
            system, and license plan. Features shown on the website or at checkout are subject to the
            applicable product description for the version and plan you purchase.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-4">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white"><span class="text-sky-400">3.</span> Eligibility and Lawful Use</h2>
          <p>
            You must be legally capable of entering into a binding contract under the laws that apply to you.
            If you are below the age of majority where you live, you may use the Software only with the
            involvement and legally valid consent of a parent or legal guardian, where permitted by law.
          </p>
          <p>
            You are responsible for confirming that your use of TradeGuard and any third-party trading
            platform is lawful in your location and complies with the platform's own terms, eligibility
            requirements, and restrictions. TradeGuard does not authorize or encourage conduct that is
            unlawful in your jurisdiction.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-4">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white"><span class="text-sky-400">4.</span> License Grant and Device Binding</h2>
          <p>
            Subject to these Terms and payment of the applicable fee, the Provider grants you a limited,
            personal, non-exclusive, non-sublicensable license to install and use the Software on one (1)
            authorized Windows PC per active license at a time, for the license period applicable to your
            plan.
          </p>
          <p>
            License keys are associated with a device identifier (HWID) for license validation and device
            allocation. You may transfer a license to a replacement PC only through the supported transfer
            process and subject to the reset or transfer allocation disclosed for your plan at checkout or
            in the account interface. Some plans may have no self-service transfer allocation. You may not
            share, resell, publish, sublicense, or simultaneously use a license on unauthorized devices.
          </p>
          <p>
            We may use reasonable technical controls to detect duplicate activation, unauthorized sharing,
            fraud, or circumvention of device limits. Information about device identifiers and related
            processing is described in our <a href="/privacy" class="text-sky-400 underline hover:text-sky-300">Privacy Policy</a>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-4">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white"><span class="text-sky-400">5.</span> License Duration, First Activation, and Stacking</h2>
          <p>
            <strong class="text-white">A paid license period begins only when the license key is first
            successfully activated and associated with an authorized device.</strong> The license period
            does not begin merely because you placed an order, completed payment, received a license key,
            or downloaded the installer. The activation timestamp recorded by the license system is used
            to calculate the license expiry time.
          </p>
          <p>
            Unless the applicable plan description at checkout states otherwise, the paid plan durations are
            seven (7) days for a 7-Day Pass, thirty (30) days for a 1-Month Pass, and three hundred sixty-five
            (365) days for a 1-Year Pass. These are consecutive 24-hour periods measured from successful
            first activation, not calendar-month anniversaries. The duration and features of the plan shown
            at checkout form part of your purchase.
          </p>
          <p>
            Where license stacking or an upgrade is offered, an eligible additional license activated on an
            authorized device may extend the remaining time of an existing active license. Stacking and
            plan-tier compatibility are subject to the rules disclosed for the applicable plans. A lower-tier
            license may not replace or downgrade an active higher-tier license. Any transfer/reset allocation
            associated with a plan is governed by the plan details shown at purchase.
          </p>
          <p>
            You are responsible for retaining your license key and activating it on the intended device.
            Activation requires an internet connection and successful communication with the license service.
            If activation fails, contact support before repeatedly attempting activation or transferring the
            license to another device.
          </p>
          <p>
            The start of the license-use period is separate from the time at which digital content or a
            download is supplied for purposes of any statutory withdrawal or cancellation right. Section 14
            and applicable law govern those rights.
          </p>
        </section>

