          </p>
          <div class="bg-slate-800/80 border-l-4 border-sky-500 p-4 rounded-r-lg space-y-3 text-xs md:text-sm">
            <strong class="text-sky-300 font-bold block">Digital Content and Withdrawal Rights</strong>
            <p>
              Depending on your location and the nature of the transaction, you may have a statutory
              withdrawal or cancellation period for an online purchase. For example, certain distance
              contracts in Taiwan may carry a seven-day right to rescind, subject to statutory exceptions.
              In the European Union, consumers generally have a fourteen-day withdrawal period for distance
              contracts, subject to applicable exceptions and conditions.
            </p>
            <p>
              For eligible digital content supplied without a tangible medium, applicable law may allow a
              withdrawal right to be lost once supply begins only if the required conditions are met. These
              may include your prior express consent to begin supply during the withdrawal period, your
              acknowledgement of the resulting loss of the withdrawal right, and our confirmation of the
              contract and consent. The requirements differ by jurisdiction.
            </p>
            <p>
              Where such consent or acknowledgement is required, it will be requested separately and clearly
              before the relevant supply begins. Your choice to have the paid license term start on first
              successful activation does not, by itself, determine when digital content is supplied or
              whether a statutory withdrawal right is lost.
            </p>
          </div>
          <p>
            To request a refund, exercise a statutory withdrawal right, or report a billing or activation
            problem, contact <a href="mailto:support@gettradeguard.app" class="text-sky-400 underline hover:text-sky-300">support@gettradeguard.app</a>
